    "summary": "High‑energy Oregon County Fair ’82 – debut West LA Fadeaway & monster Wheel→Other One",
    "review": "The August 28, 1982 Oregon County Fair show is a true high‑octane snapshot of the early‑‘80s Dead. The band bursts out of the gate with a sizzling set that includes the historic first live performance of \"West L.A. Fadeaway,\" where Jerry’s vocal shines like never before and his guitar wails through inventive turnarounds and envelope‑filter wizardry. Set 2 builds an unstoppable momentum, highlighted by a thunderous Wheel → The Other One → Truckin' sequence that many fans cite as one of the night’s fiercest jams, and an all‑time great rendition of \"Althea.\" The encore caps it off with a triumphant \"Dupree's Diamond Blues,\" leaving the crowd buzzing. Across multiple soundboard sources the mix is crystal clear and bottom‑heavy, letting Phil’s massive low‑end bass and Brent Mydland’s organ roar with almost Black Sabbath intensity while Mickey Hart and Bill Kreutzmann keep the drums on fire throughout.",
